Add the `exception_receiver` pattern to the MIPS backend of gcc 2.95.2.

The pattern follows two implementations already present in gcc 2.95.2:
  - semantics from pa/pa.md ("Load the PIC register from the stack slot
    (in our caller's frame)", gated on flag_pic);
  - form from alpha/alpha.md (define_insn + unspec_volatile + literal
    template; Alpha emits `ldgp $29,0($29)`).

The generic hook is receive_exception_label (gcc/except.c:722-738): it emits
gen_exception_receiver() at the head of every landing pad if the target defines
the pattern. pa, i386 and alpha define it; MIPS does not, so the landing pads
are entered with the $gp of the frame that threw the exception (in PIC code $gp
is call-clobbered and nothing on the unwinding path restores it).

The offset is current_frame_info.args_size, the same value that mips.c prints
in the `.cprestore` directive of the prologue.

Apply it after the three Sony patches (docker/Dockerfile.sonygcc does).
Details: docs/compiler.md. tools/check_toolchain.py pins it by sha256.

--- a/gcc/config/mips/mips.md
+++ b/gcc/config/mips/mips.md
@@ -82,6 +82,39 @@
 ;;          (const_string "default"))))
 
 ;; ??? Fix everything that tests this attribute.
+
+;; Reload the PIC register ($28) at the head of an exception landing pad.
+;;
+;; Semantics transposed from pa.md ("Load the PIC register from the stack slot
+;; (in our caller's frame)", gated on flag_pic); form from alpha.md
+;; (define_insn + unspec_volatile + literal template).  The generic hook is
+;; receive_exception_label (except.c:722-738), which emits
+;; gen_exception_receiver() at the head of EVERY landing pad if the target
+;; defines the pattern.  Three targets define it in 2.95.2 (pa, i386, alpha).
+;;
+;; It is needed because the unwinding path enters the pad WITHOUT returning
+;; from the call, so gas has not inserted the reload it attaches after every
+;; `jal' macro, and $gp is still that of the frame that threw.
+;;
+;; The offset is NOT a free parameter: it is current_frame_info.args_size, the
+;; same value that mips.c prints in the .cprestore of the prologue.
+(define_insn "exception_receiver"
+  [(unspec_volatile [(const_int 0)] 19)]
+  "TARGET_ABICALLS && !TARGET_64BIT"
+  "*
+{
+  static char retval[64];
+
+  sprintf (retval, \"lw\\t%s,%ld(%s)\",
+	   reg_names[PIC_OFFSET_TABLE_REGNUM],
+	   current_frame_info.args_size,
+	   reg_names[STACK_POINTER_REGNUM]);
+  return retval;
+}"
+  [(set_attr "type"	"load")
+   (set_attr "mode"	"SI")
+   (set_attr "length"	"1")])
+
 (define_attr "cpu"
   "default,r3000,r3900,r6000,r4000,r4100,r4300,r4600,r4650,r5000,r5400,r5900,r8000" ; pattern-sanitize-r5900-1  CYGNUS LOCAL vr5400/raeburn
   (const (symbol_ref "mips_cpu_attr")))
